Analysis of a random sample of six devices from the LQ device population shows a measurable improvement in Microsoft Edge performance following policy implementation. Average CPU utilization decreased from 0.045 to 0.027, representing approximately 40% improvement, while average memory consumption decreased from 1267 MB to 1108 MB, representing approximately 12.5% improvement. Devices with previously higher resource consumption demonstrated the most significant gains, indicating that the implemented configuration changes are effectively optimizing Microsoft Edge performance and reducing endpoint resource utilization.
